TCP/IP
  IP: Protocol, IP (Internet Protocol)  for routing a package from one address to other
  TCP: Transmission Control Protocol, Ensures all data arrives to destiny in good shape.
  - Split data into segments (packages) and numbered
  - Stablished the connection between sender and receiver before starting (three-way handshake)
  - validates each package arrvies
  - Request a resend if something is missing
  - Assamble everything in the destinatary using the package numbers
